    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2705A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to permitting Adelante of Suffolk County, Inc. to\nfile an application for a real property tax exemption\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo exempt, Adelante of Suffolk County, Inc., a not-for-profit\ncorporation from liability for payment of real property taxes due on\nthe 2007-2006 assessment roll.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill would authorize and direct the assessor of the town of Islip\nto accept applications for an exemption from real property taxes as if\nmade pursuant to section 420 of the real property tax law for the\nassessment rolls as completed in 2007-2008.  When satisfied that\nAdelante of Suffolk County, Inc. would otherwise have been entitled to\nsaid exemption, the assessor is authorized and directed to grant same,\nrefund the appropriate pro rata portion of any taxes paid and cancel\nall remaining unpaid taxes, related fines and penalties.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nAdelante of Suffolk County, Inc. is an active provider of vital\nservices to community seniors, youth and persons with special needs.\nThis property tax relief would help them to continue their work for\nthe residents of Suffolk County.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2009: New Legislation.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nA waiver of Adelante of Suffolk County, Inc.  2008 outstanding\nproperty tax liability.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
